Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/17] board: alpine-v2: boot the initrd and FDT in place

booti/bootm otherwise copy the initrd and the FDT to the top of the
first bank. The load addresses in the env already keep them clear of
the kernel and of reserved memory, so skip the copy (saves copying a
large initrd, and nothing lands near the firmware ranges). The
"don't relocate" value must be the 64-bit all-ones: 0xffffffff is
read as a 4 GiB limit on arm64.
---
 board/amazon/alpine-v2/alpine-v2.env | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/amazon/alpine-v2/alpine-v2.env b/board/amazon/alpine-v2/alpine-v2.env
--- a/board/amazon/alpine-v2/alpine-v2.env
+++ b/board/amazon/alpine-v2/alpine-v2.env
@@ -18,3 +18,9 @@ kernel_addr_r=0x10000000
 kernel_comp_addr_r=0x20000000
 kernel_comp_size=0x4000000
 ramdisk_addr_r=0x30000000
+/*
+ * Use the initrd and FDT where they were loaded (all ones, 64-bit:
+ * 0xffffffff would be a 4 GiB limit, not "don't relocate").
+ */
+fdt_high=0xffffffffffffffff
+initrd_high=0xffffffffffffffff
